# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Copy Inventory

Every user-facing string, and where it appears. The counterpart to the brand-voice
document: that one says how to write, this one says what is currently written.

**Largely a derived collateral.** `/audit-copy` reads it and the extraction tooling
regenerates the inventory, so hand-editing the generated sections loses work on the
next run. The sections marked as hand-maintained are the exceptions.

**Scope: a project that ships user-facing text of its own.** This document is an
*inventory* — the strings that exist, extracted from source. A project whose strings
belong to its consumers rather than to itself — a component library, a package — has
no inventory to take, and should not scaffold this document with a handful of its own
internal strings as though that were coverage. What such a project needs instead is
*authoring rules*: what the few strings it does ship must sound like, and what a
consumer must supply rather than inherit. That belongs in the brand-voice document,
which is about how to write, not in this one, which is about what is written.

